From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntoskrnl: Implement ObReferenceObjectByPointer.

ObReferenceObjectByPointer takes a reference on an object of the given type
(or of any type when none is given) and fails with
STATUS_OBJECT_TYPE_MISMATCH otherwise; it returned STATUS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED.

Gate: test/ntoskrnl-obref-gate.sh (a probe driver; 64-bit, a WoW64 host skips).
---
 dlls/ntoskrnl.exe/ntoskrnl.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntoskrnl.exe/ntoskrnl.c b/dlls/ntoskrnl.exe/ntoskrnl.c
index d54f553..d46bd48 100644
--- a/dlls/ntoskrnl.exe/ntoskrnl.c
+++ b/dlls/ntoskrnl.exe/ntoskrnl.c
@@ -3169,9 +3169,19 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI ObReferenceObjectByPointer(void *obj, ACCESS_MASK access,
                                            POBJECT_TYPE type,
                                            KPROCESSOR_MODE mode)
 {
-    FIXME("(%p, %lx, %p, %d): stub\n", obj, access, type, mode);
+    struct object_header *header = (struct object_header *)obj - 1;
 
-    return STATUS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED;
+    TRACE("(%p, %lx, %p, %d)\n", obj, access, type, mode);
+
+    /* "STATUS_OBJECT_TYPE_MISMATCH if the object is not of the given type";
+     * a kernel-mode reference is not checked for access */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_OBREF_NO_TYPECHECK
+    if (type && header->type != type) return STATUS_OBJECT_TYPE_MISMATCH;
+#else
+    (void)header;
+#endif
+    ObReferenceObject( obj );
+    return STATUS_SUCCESS;
 }
 
 
